```plaintext
2result.sql
```

Reason:  
• 0result.sql ignores the stratum‐level expansion factor and therefore produces acreages that are orders of magnitude too small.  
• 1result.sql omits the condition‑level proportion multiplier and thus over/under‑states acres; its join logic nevertheless yields implausibly low totals (e.g. 16 M ac forest for Texas while large western and southeastern states are much larger).  
• 2result.sql keeps only the latest EXPCURR evaluation‑group per state, multiplies expansion_factor × adjustment_factor × condition_proportion_unadjusted for both MACR and SUBP bases, and applies the correct timberland/forestland filters. Because it includes every required component of the acreage calculation and produces realistic statewide totals, it is the most correct of the three.